* Add more filesystem options to mkfs.briefs as they become available.
* Implement the remaining ioctls in the FUSE bridge: the file-range
  exchange ioctls (XFS_IOC_EXCHANGE_RANGE/SWAP_RANGE and COMMIT_RANGE —
  a ~500-line two-inode port of the kernel's briefs_do_exchange;
  rationale in fuse/ioctl_mount.go). O_TMPFILE is not bridge-addressable
  (the 6.12 FUSE client has no O_TMPFILE support), and neither is
  FS_IOC_FIEMAP: the 6.12 VFS intercepts it (do_vfs_ioctl routes it to
  inode->i_op->fiemap, which fs/fuse does not implement) so the caller
  gets EOPNOTSUPP with no FUSE round trip, and even a forwarding client
  would cap the restricted-mode transfer at _IOC_SIZE(cmd) = 32 bytes,
  the struct fiemap header alone. generic/032 stays NOT RUN, same
  blocker class as O_TMPFILE.
* [Done for xfstests] mkfs.briefs and fsck.briefs command line flags are
  sufficiently xfstests-compatible (force flag `-f`, check-only default,
  `-r -y` repair shape). Further standards alignment may be useful.
